I2AtHZ2LOI8OQ","name":"Maurepas Foods","shared_categories":"American (New), Restaurants","shared_category_count":2},{"business_id":"kdqoDMuvyNedsouc1i33vQ","name":"Araña Taqueria y Cantina","shared_categories":"Restaurants","shared_category_count":1},{"business_id":"mhrW9O0O5hXGXGnEYBVoag","name":"Jacques-Imo's Cafe","shared_categories":"Restaurants","shared_category_count":1},{"business_id":"Zi-F-YvyVOK0k5QD7lrLOg","name":"Muriel's Jackson Square","shared_categories":"Restaurants","shared_category_count":1},{"business_id":"_Bi9kN_eR75G1eqIl7S3pA","name":"The Bulldog","shared_categories":"Restaurants","shared_category_count":1},{"business_id":"AU-B663F3MPO7W-goWwwXA","name":"B Mac's","shared_categories":"","shared_category_count":0},{"business_id":"pKykk7lnD6Tf9wSzJYRyJA","name":"Starbucks","shared_categories":"","shared_category_count":0}],"text":[{"business_id":"JRa60aO_ZZCdfDIU6IlpCA","review_id":"yYjPMOnuzYWmXxwWFCWREQ","date":"2018-06-15T06:20:38","stars":5,"text_representativeness":0.9322791695594788,"text_excerpt":"Went twice on my recent trip to NOLA. Service was great both times, super nice and attentive staff. Had the mussels one night- the server told me it was more like an entree portion, which was appreciated because they were right. Lots of food and it was really good. The octopus appetizer wasn't my favorite thing. The tartness of the pickled turnips overpowered the rest of the dish. The octopus itself and the grilled tomatoes were really good though. Finally, I don't want to oversell anyone on this but good fuckin' god the charred beet appetizer was amazing. I was in town for almost a week and it was the best thing I ate. I went back specifically for that and both times the first bite blew ..."},{"business_id":"JRa60aO_ZZCdfDIU6IlpCA","review_id":"F_oDgbl06C0SHjnyyF833Q","date":"2016-04-25T01:22:55","stars":5,"text_representativeness":0.9268603324890137,"text_excerpt":"Came here for happy hour. Loved the bartender. My dude and I were playing Beanboozled and she was down to play too. She ended up getting Rotten Eggs and Canned Dog Food but was so cool about it. Wish I could remember her name, but she gets 5 stars! Anyway. Happy hour. Oysters. $1 each. They were so big and juicy and we watched the guy shuck the oysters so we knew they were fresh! They're served with cocktail sauce and a mignonette. French Fries. $3. Just regular fat fries. They were served with ketchup and some kind of mayo. The mayo was really good. I don't eat mayo. So trust me. It was really good. Or maybe it wasn't mayo? Lol. Fried cauliflower. $8. Very flavorful. But probably wouldn'..."},{"business_id":"JRa60aO_ZZCdfDIU6IlpCA","review_id":"ZsTdABESBXcrEqXz3AYuPA","date":"2017-09-21T15:11:21","stars":5,"text_representativeness":0.9265933036804199,"text_excerpt":"One of my more memorable meals in New Orleans. Not 'excellent' at any one thing, yet truly very good all around. The service was great and friendly, the menu simple to digest and with plenty of tasty options for everyone, a relaxing and interesting decor and vibe. We started with the pan roasted shrimp, which are insanely good and not to be missed. I followed that with the strip steak and bone marrow for my main. Pinch me. Am I dreaming? No, seriously...they serve a pretty darn good strip steak accompanied by a huge marrow bone. OK. Pinch me. Nope, it's real. I washed it all down with a ginger beer and went back for dessert. The coffee crème brûlée was seriously unreal. I never gave Balis..."}],"visual":[{"business_id":"JRa60aO_ZZCdfDIU6IlpCA","photo_id":"PzuZ6BPBscLmMudBUCqW7g","label":"inside","image_url":"/photos/PzuZ6BPBscLmMudBUCqW7g.jpg","visual_representativeness":0.9090521335601807},{"business_id":"JRa60aO_ZZCdfDIU6IlpCA","photo_id":"_MuBvlxCMwYvs6-MLG7vtw","label":"food","image_url":"/photos/_MuBvlxCMwYvs6-MLG7vtw.jpg","visual_representativeness":0.8444976806640625},{"business_id":"JRa60aO_ZZCdfDIU6IlpCA","photo_id":"ZKAaFabxm0DTOAFl6XeWTg","label":"food","image_url":"/photo